Z||000000||87ECO5||02-13-2001||03:05 PM||||Sorry if this has been covered already ...<P>Cliff, I was running a search a few minutes ago and discovered something that confused me.<P>After a search completes and lists out the topics matching your criteria, the topic title is listed along with a few other columns - including a "name" column.  Now, when viewing the threads in each section, the name in the "name" (or "topic starter") column is just that - the name of the person that started the thread.  However, the name displayed in the "name" column of the search results is NOT the topic starter.  What is it?  I can't figure out a pattern.<P>Sorry - slow day at work ...||||reg||5
Z||000001||TheFiero64||02-13-2001||03:27 PM||||It's the first person that mentions the word you are searching for.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||02-13-2001||03:42 PM||||TheFiero64 is correct. That's exactly what it is. )||||reg||1
